## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (line 87)

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`  
**Research ref:** Camara et al. (SAST 2021) — correlated with flaky tests  
**Integration calibration:** Still flagged HIGH. Even integration tests should not use unconditional `Thread.Sleep`; this makes the suite 3 seconds slower and non-deterministic on slow CI agents.

```csharp
// SMELL
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with timeout:**
```csharp
var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
{
    if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
        return;
    await Task.Delay(100);
}
Assert.Fail("Notification was not sent within 5 seconds.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky test failures under load; unnecessarily slow suite.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (lines 101–108)

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`

```csharp
// SMELL — different assertions execute depending on runtime type
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix — assert what the test actually expects; separate type variants:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_ReturnsStandardUser_WithCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch may never execute — hidden testing gap; diagnosis is ambiguous on failure.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (lines 113–119)

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`

```csharp
// SMELL — no assertion; passes even if inserts silently corrupt data
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix — verify the effect:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — test reports green while data integrity issues go undetected.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (lines 35–38)

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`

```csharp
// SMELL — 4 assertions, no messages; failure output is ambiguous
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add discriminating messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive Id");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** When CI fails you get `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` with no indication of which property or why.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured:

| Method | Notes |
|--------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert; focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single-concern; negative assertion is appropriate |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count after 3 inserts is self-documenting (not Magic Number) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimately exercises concurrency; asserts outcome |

The in-memory SQLite fixture is **not** a Mystery Guest — it's hermetic, fast, and self-contained. The `_connection`/`_repository` setup is used by all tests, so there is **no General Fixture** smell.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Split into type-specific test methods |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop or `TaskCompletionSource` |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Add message strings to assertions in `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` |

Fixes 1–2 prevent **false-pass risk** (tests passing when they shouldn't). Fix 3 prevents **flakiness**. Fix 4 improves **diagnosability**.
